   373	def render(inst: dict) -> str:
   374	    exponents = ", ".join(str(v) for v in inst["power_exponents"])
   375	    text = f"""Four prime squares and 46 powers of two
   376	
   377	An integer is prime if it is greater than 1 and its only positive divisors are
   378	1 and itself.  Find exactly four pairwise distinct prime integers
   379	p0 < p1 < p2 < p3, each in the inclusive interval
   380	[{inst['prime_lower']}, {inst['prime_upper']}], such that
   381	
   382	  p0^2 + p1^2 + p2^2 + p3^2 + sum(2^e for e in E) = N.
   383	
   384	The fixed list E contains exactly 46 exponents; repeated exponents are allowed:
   385	  E = [{exponents}]
   386	
   387	Instance checksums (ordinary base-10 integers):
   388	  sum(2^e for e in E) = {inst['power_total']}
   389	  N = {inst['target']}
   390	  required prime-square subtotal = N - sum(2^e for e in E)
   391	                                 = {inst['prime_square_target']}
   392	
   393	The order of E has no significance.  The four output primes must be written in
   394	strictly increasing order; no repeats and no values outside the inclusive
   395	interval are allowed.  Any quadruple satisfying all these conditions is valid.
   396	
   397	Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as four comma-separated
   398	base-10 integers.
   399	Example: <answer>101, 151, 197, 251</answer>
   400	Output nothing else inside the tags."""
   401	    mode = os.environ.get("GV_HINT_MODE")
   402	    if mode == "structural":
   403	        text += "\n\nHint: " + STRUCTURAL_HINT
   404	    elif mode == "placebo":
   405	        text += "\n\nHint: " + PLACEBO_HINT
   406	    return text
