   178	- The hidden arithmetic progression is a generator feature, not a conclusion of the
   179	  paper. Track B measures whether a solver discovers and executes that compression.
   180	- The 0/250,000 density estimate is relative to uniformly random increasing
   181	  four-subsets of all primes in the interval. It gives an upper-resolution statement
   182	  (“below roughly one in 250,000 was observed”), not an exact solution density and
   183	  not a complexity proof.
   184	- The panel did not run LLL, an optimized low-memory four-sum, quadratic-form
   185	  algorithms, or a construction-aware scan of all 50 wheel gaps; the last is the
   186	  intended compact route and is expected to succeed with tools.
