codex
The structure-aware audit exposed another important consequence: at the current \(10^{10}\) prime scale, the target and interval determine the sum of the four primes exactly. Combined with the AP hint, that collapses the intended 50-gap scan to a direct moment calculation, so the claimed 274-operation route is overstated. I’m testing a lower prime scale where the sum remains genuinely ambiguous while the generic four-sum baseline still costs millions of operations; this is exactly the kind of “what makes it easy” check Step 0 requires.
